<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13267" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποναίω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>remove, send away,</i> used by <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in aor. I, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς ἂν . . περικαλλέα κούρην ἂψ
					ἀπονάσσωσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.86
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1492
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i>wend one's way back,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δουλίχιόνδ᾽ ἀπενάσσατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.629
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.254
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			aor.
			
				Med.
			 in trans. sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπενάσσατο
				παῖδα</span>
			<i>sent away her</i> child, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1260
			</span></i>(lyr.):—
				Pass.
			, aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονασθῆναι,</span>
			<i>to be taken away, depart from</i> a place, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σᾶς πατρίδος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				175
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πατρὸς καὶ πόλεως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Med.</u>
					166
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
